-- title:
--   v-adic valuation as ofAdd of minus countᵥ
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a Dedekind domain, let $K$ be a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $R$, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $R$ (an element of `HeightOneSpectrum R`), and let $x \in K$ be nonzero. The assertion is an identity in $\mathbb{Z}_{m0} =$ `WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)`: the value $v(x)$ of Mathlib's multiplicative $v$-adic valuation `IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuation K v` at $x$ equals the image under `Multiplicative.ofAdd`, coerced into `WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)`, of $-\,\mathrm{count}_v\bigl((x)\bigr)$, where $\mathrm{count}_v$ is `FractionalIdeal.count K v`, the integer exponent of $v$ in the factorisation of a nonzero fractional ideal, and $(x)$ is the principal fractional ideal `FractionalIdeal.spanSingleton R⁰ x` generated by $x$ over the non-zero-divisors of $R$. Thus the additive $v$-adic order of $x$, normalised so that a uniformiser has valuation $\mathrm{ofAdd}(-1)$, is exactly the exponent of $v$ in $(x)$.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the two parallel notions of $v$-adic order available for a Dedekind domain: the multiplicative $\mathbb{Z}_{m0}$-valued valuation attached to a height-one prime and the integer exponent of that prime in the factorisation of a fractional ideal, compared on principal fractional ideals. It is used in the level-arithmetic part of the development, where $S$-unit computations are translated between ideal-theoretic factorisations and valuations.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDedekindDomain_HeightOneSpectrum_valuation_eq_ofAdd_neg_count_spanSingleton.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open IsDedekindDomain FractionalIdeal
open scoped nonZeroDivisors

theorem IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuation_eq_ofAdd_neg_count_spanSingleton
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDedekindDomain R] {K : Type*} [Field K]
    [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] (v : HeightOneSpectrum R) (x : K) (hx : x ≠ 0) :
    v.valuation K x =
      (↑(Multiplicative.ofAdd (-(FractionalIdeal.count K v (FractionalIdeal.spanSingleton R⁰ x)))) :
        WithZero (Multiplicative ℤ)) := by sorry
